WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.002
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Andy Cohen.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.304
So obviously, New York has a new
mayor but, even more exciting,

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.573
a new cast
of New York Housewives.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.742
-Yes, this is a big deal.
-It's a huge deal.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.545
-Wow, I didn't know where
you were going with that.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:17.083
My God. By the way,
there is a Housewife,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.652
a former Housewife
in the universe

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.722
who I found out today has
a major crush on Seth Meyers.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.859
-Really?
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.428
She is a former peach holder

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:31.130
from "The Real Housewives
of Atlanta."

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.299
-Okay.
-She is Phaedra Parks.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.633
-Phaedra Parks?
-Yes.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.770
She is an attorney at law
and a mortician.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.106
And she likes you.
-Wow! That is great.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.808
-She could handle
your legal bills.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.409
And she could plan your funeral.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:44.877
-Yeah.
-Yes. Absolutely.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.179
-I was going to say, if there's
a funeral she needs to plan,

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.180
it's my wife's.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.082
-Well, I was going to say that,

00:00:50.082 --> 00:00:51.851
but I didn't want to.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.155
-That's really kind.
That's your host at heart.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.291
You left the nicer joke for me.
-I did. I did.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.959
I also -- I was like,
am I going to make a joke

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:02.428
about his wife like that?

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.730
It's like, I'm not --
I don't think I'm doing that.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.998
Yes.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:08.234
-I'm realizing your restraint

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.102
was probably the smarter
of the two paths.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.338
-Well, by the way,
not a great week

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.641
to make jokes
about people's wives.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.875
-No.
-Yes.

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.646
-So, you are no stranger
to slaps.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.080
-Yes.
-In the "Housewife" universe.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.415
-That is true.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:26.218
You've seen,
you've observed tempers rising

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:29.655
and someone making the terrible
decision to slap someone else.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:31.490
-Yes, I have.
-Do you --

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.093
-Where are you going with this?
-Do you think this is --

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:36.329
I mean, obviously,
these two people were friends.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:40.399
Do you think there's a chance,
even after the stage slap --

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:41.501
-That they could come together?
-Yeah.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.636
-Oh, my God, well,
I live in a universe

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:47.673
where Housewives do and say
terrible things to each other.

00:01:47.673 --> 00:01:49.676
And then they're like,
"You know what?

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.310
I think we're gonna be okay."
-Yeah.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:54.447
-Yeah, so in my universe, yes.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.083
-I think there is a path out.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.117
-I do, too.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:01.187
-I think we fix this.
-Yes.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.590
-Now, unfortunately,
we all had to watch it.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.191
-That is true.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.461
-What's the worst heckling
experience you've ever had?

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:12.031
The very worst, where you
were, like, shaky after?

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:16.302
-I -- My improv partner and I
did the mistake.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.471
We were in Edinburgh
at the Fringe Festival,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.506
and we performed
at a stand-up night,

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.074
and so it was
a Scottish audience,

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:24.343
and we tried to do, like,
American improv.

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:26.945
We were asking Scots
late at night for suggestions,

00:02:26.945 --> 00:02:29.215
and they were very angry.
-Right.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.549
-And I remember
at the end of the night,

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.685
the emcee was naming
all the acts,

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.121
and when he said our names,
it was dead silent.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.990
-Wow.
-And then one guy just went,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.658
"[Bleep]"

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.825
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:41.928
And it was like --
it was so solitary,

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.530
as if they had agreed
ahead of time,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.866
no one will say anything
and then, whatever,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.500
Pat over here will yell,
"[Bleep]"

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.735
-Right.
Right.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:51.971
-So that was probably --
-That was it, yes.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.774
-You've also got --
You've got a "Real Housewives"

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.843
not just new here in New York.
-Right.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.445
-But Dubai.
-Dubai. Dubai.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.013
-How'd you pick?
Why Dubai?

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:04.016
-I just watched the first
episode this very day,

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.285
as a matter of fact.
It was really exciting.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:10.222
You know, I think Dubai --
when you deal with a city

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.224
that winds up making
Beverly Hills

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.494
look, like, pedantic...
-Yeah.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.828
-...it's kind of -- you're like,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.530
"Oh, well,
I'm paying attention here.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.866
So I'm excited for --
It's a totally different --

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.068
And I think there are
a lot of people

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:25.471
who have ideas about Dubai that,

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.506
you know,
all women are X, Y, or Z.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:29.041
And this is really going to
blow the lid

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.610
off of a lot
of preconceived notions.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.012
-Yeah, that's true.
-So to speak, yeah.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.513
-I'm not even realizing.
I'm like, "Oh, yeah.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.248
I would have a lot
of preconceived notions."

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:37.750
And then how much of it --

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.652
Obviously, you pick a place,
and that's a huge part of it.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.688
-Right.
-Having done all these seasons,

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.223
how quickly do you realize
you've nailed it with the cast?

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.258
That you've gotten the right
people to be engaging?

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:49.495
-I mean, typically we don't
launch until we have a cast

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.731
that we feel like
is a great cast and we love.

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:55.134
But, I mean, usually,
you can tell pretty quickly.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.202
I mean, they make you laugh.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.071
I mean, these women
are superstars.

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.906
It's why we're still going
16 years later.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:03.109
And the New York thing,
it's super exciting.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.710
We announced a couple weeks ago,

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.880
we are recasting "The Real
Housewives of New York City"

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.416
from the ground up.
-Yeah.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.685
-And what an exciting
thing to do,

00:04:13.685 --> 00:04:16.923
because there are so many
stories to be told in New York

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.158
and so many that
we haven't told yet.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:22.595
-Is there a higher standard
when you're doing New York?

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.864
Like, do you feel
a little bit more anxiety

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.132
about trying to do that again?

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.667
-I mean,
we just want to find stars.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.069
We just want
to find great people.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.170
-That's exciting.
-Yeah. Yes.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.538
-And they must, at this point --

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.740
the other nice thing is
you've had this go on so long,

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.177
this franchise, people must be
so excited to be a part of it.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.078
-They are.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.446
-There are two types of people.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.548
People who want to be
on the "Housewives"

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.884
and people who don't, yes.

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.820
We are looking for the ones
who want to appear.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.288
-They're like,
"I'll be on your show,

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.457
but I'd like to keep my private
life and my work life separate."

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.993
-Yeah.
Oh, yeah, yeah, exactly. Great!

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.261
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.228
-Thanks, man.
Great to see you.

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:57.730
-Guys, that's Andy Cohen.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.365
"Watch What Happens Live
with Andy Cohen"

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.367
airs Sunday through
Thursday nights on Bravo.

